1,166.71 406.18,165.75 410.35,164.80 414.52,163.84 418.69,162.89 422.86,161.93 427.04,160.98 431.21,160.03 435.38,159.07 439.55,158.12 443.72,157.16 447.89,156.21 452.06,155.25 456.23,154.30 460.40,153.34 464.57,152.39 468.74,151.43 472.91,150.48 477.09,149.52 481.26,148.57 485.43,147.61 489.60,146.66 493.77,145.70 497.94,144.75 502.11,143.79 506.28,142.84 510.45,141.88 514.62,140.93 518.79,139.97 522.96,139.02 527.14,138.07 531.31,137.11 535.48,136.16 539.65,135.20 543.82,134.25 547.99,133.29 552.16,132.34 556.33,131.38 560.50,130.43 564.67,129.47 568.84,128.52 573.02,127.56 577.19,126.61 581.36,125.65 585.53,124.70 589.70,123.74 593.87,122.79 598.04,121.83 602.21,120.88 606.38,119.92 610.55,118.97 614.72,118.02 618.89,117.06 623.07,116.11 627.24,115.15 631.41,114.20 635.58,113.24 639.75,112.29 643.92,111.33 648.09,110.38 652.26,109.42 656.43,108.47 660.60,107.51 664.77,106.56 668.94,105.60 673.12,104.65 677.29,103.69 681.46,102.74 685.63,101.78 689.80,100.83 693.97,99.87 698.14,98.92 702.31,97.96 706.48,97.01 710.65,96.06 714.82,95.10 718.99,94.15 723.17,93.19 727.34,92.24 731.51,91.28 735.68,90.33 739.85,89.37 744.02,88.42 748.19,87.46 752.36,86.51 756.53,85.55 760.70,84.60 764.87,83.64 769.05,82.69 773.22,81.73 777.39,80.78 781.56,79.82 785.73,78.87 789.90,77.91 794.07,76.96 798.24,76.01 802.41,75.05 806.58,74.10 810.75,73.14 814.92,72.19 819.10,71.23 823.27,70.28 827.44,69.32 831.61,68.37 835.78,67.41 839.95,66.46 844.12,65.50 848.29,64.55 852.46,63.59 856.63,62.64 860.80,61.68 864.97,60.73 869.15,59.77 873.32,58.82 877.49,57.86 881.66,56.91 885.83,55.95 890.00,55.00\"/><text x=\"65\" y=\"329\" fill=\"#b65b09\" font-size=\"14\">Per-office rainfall scenario</text></svg><button class=\"export-btn\" type=\"button\" data-csv=\"Formula,Budget units moved from current allocation,Offices assigned zero units,Offices retaining one unit\nEqual allocation (observed),0,0,199\n&quot;Province mean, then split among DEOs (existing scenario)&quot;,44,44,120\nEach DEO weighted by province mean (alternative),0,0,199\nEach DEO weighted by province median (sensitivity),0,0,199\n\">Export CSV</button><div class=\"evidence-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Formula</th><th>Budget units moved from current allocation</th><th>Offices assigned zero units</th><th>Offices retaining one unit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Equal allocation (observed)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>199</td></tr><tr><td>Province mean, then split among DEOs (existing scenario)</td><td>44</td><td>44</td><td>120</td></tr><tr><td>Each DEO weighted by province mean (alternative)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>199</td></tr><tr><td>Each DEO weighted by province median (sensitivity)</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>199</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Units moved = half the sum of absolute changes; all scenarios conserve 199 budget units. Largest-remainder rounding uses office name to break ties. A budget unit is not a verified count of installed collectors. Province means are shared proxies, not 199 independent rainfall observations.</p><p class=\"caution\">Hypothesis for investigators: the flat amount is a standard package rather than a needs-based allocation. Alternatives include a minimum-coverage policy or common construction specification. Pearson correlation is undefined because every allocation is identical; a p-value against an invented random-allocation process would be misleading. Neither rainfall formula is a recommended final budget, and a model assigning zero units is not evidence an office needs none.</p><p>Mean versus median weighting changes whole-unit recommendations for 0 offices. 1 office uses a regional rainfall fallback. Establish the actual site/catchment area, design capacity, water demand, storage, access and existing assets before making a needs claim.</p><p class=\"caution\">The direct per-office rainfall formula rounds to one whole budget unit for every office, even though fractional shares differ. Equal whole units therefore do not, by themselves, refute rainfall weighting at this budget-unit resolution. The existing province-first scenario moves 44 units because provinces receive a share before it is divided among offices. That structural choice must be justified before claiming it is a better allocation.</p></section>",
      "rcs-stage-evidence": "<section id=\"rcs-stage-evidence\" class=\"investigation-evidence\"><h2>Even distribution · did any RCS allocation disappear in HGAB?</h2><p><strong>The observed budget pattern is identical distribution: 199 DEO lines at ₱4.2M each. No differentiated needs weighting is visible in those line amounts.</strong> Whether planners considered need outside the schedule requires policy/design records; equal figures alone cannot establish what they thought.</p><svg class=\"evidence-graphic\" viewBox=\"0 0 900 110\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"199 NEP RCS office lines remain unchanged in HGAB\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"15\" width=\"330\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#355b92\"/><text x=\"30\" y=\"58\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"22\">NEP: 199 × ₱4.2M</text><path d=\"M355 50 H510\" stroke=\"#18303b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><path d=\"M495 40 L515 50 L495 60\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#18303b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><rect x=\"530\" y=\"15\" width=\"350\" height=\"70\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#087e78\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"58\" fill=\"white\" font-size=\"22\">HGAB: 199 × ₱4.2M</text></svg><button class=\"export-btn\" type=\"button\" data-csv=\"Stage check,DEO RCS lines\nRetained unchanged in HGAB,199\nNo selected HGAB counterpart,0\nAllocation decreases in HGAB,0\n\">Export CSV</button><div class=\"evidence-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage check</th><th>DEO RCS lines</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Retained unchanged in HGAB</td><td>199</td></tr><tr><td>No selected HGAB counterpart</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>Allocation decreases in HGAB</td><td>0</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a class=\"export-btn\" href=\"rcs-stage-trace.csv\" download>Export all 199 RCS stage/scenario lines CSV</a> · <a href=\"rcs-stage-trace.json\">Source and LEG reference evidence JSON</a></p><p class=\"caution\">No DEO RCS line was lost in the current HGAB trace. A named LEG cannot be declared a recipient or loser without the installation locations, applicable boundaries and evidence of the funded service area.</p></section>"
    },
    "dpwh-hgab.html": {
      "hgab-investigation-evidence": "<section id=\"hgab-investigation-evidence\" class=\"investigation-evidence\"><h2>Insertion candidates · what the matching can establish</h2><p>These four statuses partition native HGAB rows; they are not four certified outcomes. Schedule totals can reconcile while individual titles, offices or occurrence links remain wrong.</p><button class=\"export-btn\" type=\"button\" data-csv=\"NEP counterpart screen,Native HGAB allocation records\nExact normalized title found in NEP,9626\nPlausible NEP title counterpart; review scope,540\nNo plausible NEP title counterpart; review candidate,5553\nMultiple or already paired NEP counterparts; review scope,556\n\">Export CSV</button><div class=\"evidence-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>NEP counterpart screen</th><th>Native HGAB allocation records</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Exact normalized title found in NEP</td><td>9626</td></tr><tr><td>Plausible NEP title counterpart; review scope</td><td>540</td></tr><tr><td>No plausible NEP title counterpart; review candidate</td><td>5553</td></tr><tr><td>Multiple or already paired NEP counterparts; review scope</td><td>556</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>5,491 domestic candidate lines carry ₱149.559B. The 4 unpaired FAP lines carrying ₱806.910M remain a separate review. Neither bucket is proof of insertion; new wording, combined occurrences or parser fragments can hide existing NEP projects.</p><p class=\"caution\">Investigators should manually audit a stratified sample by program, office class and amount band, oversampling high-value candidates, and review original NEP/HGAB pages. Report adjudicated false-positive rates with uncertainty before extrapolating. The supplied analyst export has 5,797 comparison rows, not 5,837 certified added projects; grouped rows and non-project headers use different count units.</p></section>"
    },
    "congress.html": {
      "congress-investigation-evidence": "<section id=\"congress-investigation-evidence\" class=\"investigation-evidence\"><h2>Ranking coverage and location exclusions</h2><p>Strict attribution covers 11,570/16,275 source lines (71.1%) and 52.6% of extracted allocation value. The remaining money is excluded from strict LEG rankings, not missing from the budget.</p><button class=\"export-btn\" type=\"button\" data-csv=\"Attribution outcome,HGAB lines,Allocation pesos\nStrict single LEG,11570,308912558000\nShared or unresolved,4705,278163103000\n\">Export CSV</button><div class=\"evidence-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Attribution outcome</th><th>HGAB lines</th><th>Allocation pesos</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strict single LEG</td><td>11570</td><td>₱308,912,558,000</td></tr><tr><td>Shared or unresolved</td><td>4705</td><td>₱278,163,103,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"caution\">District totals are evidence-supported lower coverage totals, not complete receipts or amounts sponsored by representatives. Offices are not legislative seats. Homonymous places require parent and geographic level; multi-place routes cannot be allocated to one LEG without segment evidence. The ₱1.2B Butuan/RTR project is a confirmed multi-place exclusion, not a Butuan-only allocation.</p><p>Before comparing districts, measure each district’s unresolved coverage using project locations and dated boundaries. Province splits, current versus historical names, shared DEOs and school names can all change eligibility for attribution. No concentration test is reliable while missing attribution differs by district.</p></section>"
    },
    "budget-innovations.html": {
      "innovation-investigation-evidence": "<section id=\"innovation-investigation-evidence\" class=\"investigation-evidence\"><h2>Returning labels · INSPIRE funding history</h2><p>INSPIRE is a returning named project, not a keyword appearing for the first time. Separate history of wording from history of funded scope.</p><button class=\"export-btn\" type=\"button\" data-csv=\"Stage/year,Observed allocation pesos\nGAA 2023,300000000\nGAA 2025,100000000\nNEP 2027,835000000\n\">Export CSV</button><div class=\"evidence-table\"><table><thead><tr><th>Stage/year</th><th>Observed allocation pesos</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>GAA 2023</td><td>₱300,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>GAA 2025</td><td>₱100,000,000</td></tr><tr><td>NEP 2027</td><td>₱835,000,000</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=\"caution\">Past enacted allocations plus a new proposal do not establish duplicate spending, actual release or disbursement. Ask for approved total project cost, component scope, procurement phases, progress, obligations and remaining balance. A newly seen phrase can also name a long-negotiated foreign-assisted project; keyword novelty is not an insertion finding.</p></section>"
    }
  }
}
